From 64c2e29a42d960f9ca14982d06f8c8ddedb4a3c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilia Sharin <isharin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:12:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] proto(sound): one multi-stream FIR pass + SIMD kernels
 for the channel decimators

FilterDecimator::getOutputs evaluates decimators that share an output
instant and a coefficient row pair in one pass over the taps
(DecimatorDot: NEON / SSE2 kernels with a scalar fallback). The history
ring is stored newest-first so the taps load forward. Every kernel keeps
the original summation order and the compilers' multiply-add contraction
rule, so the output is bit-identical (DecimatorDot_Test, golden digests,
the A/B renders of the quality harness).

Users: Ym2203Pair::renderChannels (ZX-MultiSound, 8 streams), the TSFM
board (6), the TurboSound / AY device (4).

Ym2203PairQuality_Test (DISABLED_ tools): trace capture of real tunes and
synthetic worst cases, renders for the A/B comparison.

Prototype, docs/inprogress/2026-10-03-zx-multisound/ym-decimator-prototype.md
